---
import { CACHE_CONTROL } from '@/utils/cache-control'
import { SITE_DOMAIN } from '@/utils/meta'
import PageIntro from '@/components/PageIntro.astro'
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

export const prerender = true

Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', CACHE_CONTROL.staticPage)
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FlexiThyme privacy"
  description="How FlexiThyme stores work sessions, syncs a private time bank with iCloud, supplies widgets, exports user-requested files, and removes data."
  url={`${SITE_DOMAIN}/apps/flexithyme/privacy`}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <PageIntro
      eyebrow="FlexiThyme / Privacy"
      title="Your work history stays yours."
      description="FlexiThyme has no account, advertising, analytics, or tracking. Its job is to maintain your time bank on your devices."
    />

    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-12 max-w-none">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 29 July 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who operates FlexiThyme</h2>
      <p>
        FlexiThyme is an independent app operated by Loke in Sweden. Privacy and
        support questions can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:hi@loke.dev?subject=FlexiThyme%20privacy">hi@loke.dev</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Data the app stores</h2>
      <p>
        FlexiThyme stores the work sessions, break durations, notes, balance
        adjustments, weekly schedules, starting balance, and app settings that
        you enter. This information is stored on your device using Apple
        SwiftData.
      </p>
      <p>
        A small snapshot containing the current balance, today's totals, timer
        state, and update time is kept in the app's shared Apple App Group
        container. The iOS and macOS widgets use that snapshot to show current
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Private iCloud sync</h2>
      <p>
        When available, Apple CloudKit syncs FlexiThyme records through your
        private iCloud database. The developer does not receive or query that
        private database. Apple processes the synced records under your Apple
        Account and Apple's terms and privacy policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        If the iCloud-backed store cannot open, FlexiThyme may use local-only
        storage and shows that state in the app. If persistent storage is
        unavailable, the app clearly warns that temporary changes will be lost
        when it closes.
      </p>

      <h2>No developer analytics or advertising</h2>
      <p>
        FlexiThyme does not create an app account and does not include
        advertising, tracking, analytics, or third-party crash-reporting SDKs.
        It does not sell work-history data or transmit that history to the
        developer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Apple may process device diagnostics, App Store information, Siri or
        Shortcuts requests, and iCloud traffic according to your device settings
        and Apple's privacy terms. That platform processing is not an app-owned
        tracking system.
      </p>

      <h2>User-requested exports</h2>
      <p>
        A weekly or monthly CSV report is created only after you choose Export
        CSV. The system share sheet lets you select where it goes. FlexiThyme
        does not upload the exported file to the developer.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also choose <strong>Export data archive</strong> in Settings to create
        a complete JSON copy of work sessions, notes, adjustments, schedule history,
        and settings. This file is created only when you request it and goes only
        to the destination you select in the system share sheet. Because it can contain
        notes, protect it like other private work records.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Your records remain on your devices and, when enabled, in your private
        iCloud database until you edit or delete them. Choosing <strong
          >Erase all FlexiThyme data</strong
        >
        removes work sessions, adjustments, schedules, and settings from the local
        time bank and schedules the corresponding private iCloud deletions. The app
        then returns to first-run setup.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions and changes</h2>
      <p>
        Contact <a href="mailto:hi@loke.dev?subject=FlexiThyme%20privacy"
          >hi@loke.dev</a
        >
        with a privacy question. Because the developer does not operate an app account
        or receive the private time bank, requests about records stored in iCloud
        normally need to be handled from the app or through your Apple Account.
      </p>
      <p>
        This notice may be updated when FlexiThyme's storage, sync, or
        third-party services change. The current version will remain at this
        address.
      </p>

      <p>
        For app help, visit <a href="/apps/flexithyme/support"
          >FlexiThyme support</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
